# THE EARLY HALF OF THE PNPM LOCK (#2958, #2897's follow-up).
#
# `preinstall` (scripts/refuse-other-installers.ts) refuses an `npm install`, but only AFTER npm has fetched and extracted the whole
# tree and written package-lock.json: a lifecycle script cannot run earlier. npm checks a manifest's `engines` BEFORE it fetches, and
# with this switch on it stops there (EBADENGINE) instead of warning. package.json's `engines.npm` is a range no npm satisfies, and
# its text is the message npm prints: the two are one mechanism, and neither refuses anything without the other.
#
# pnpm reads this file too, and for pnpm the switch is GLOBAL: it also refuses a dependency whose `engines.node` the running node does
# not satisfy (it ignores `engines.npm`). The lockfile's ranges were read against the nodes in use, and the read is on #2958.
engine-strict=true
